. ClusterIP (Internal Access Only)

This is the default service type. It provides a stable IP address accessible only from within the cluster.
YAML

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: my-clusterip-service
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: apache  # Must match the labels in your Deployment
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80       # Port accessible on the Service IP
      targetPort: 80 # Port the container is listening on




2. NodePort (External Access via Node IP)

This exposes the service on a specific port (30000-32767) on every Node’s IP.
YAML

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: my-nodeport-service
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: apache
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80
      targetPort: 80
      nodePort: 30001 # Optional: K8s will assign one if omitted




3. LoadBalancer (External Access via Cloud Provider)

This creates a NodePort and ClusterIP service automatically and requests an external Load Balancer from the cloud provider (e.g., AWS, GCP, Azure).
YAML

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: my-loadbalancer-service
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  selector:
    app: apache
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80
      targetPort: 80





